WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.213
As Aladdin neared the main gate of the palace, he heard trumpets.

2
00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:09.190
The gate swung open, and the sultan greeted him.

3
00:00:09.191 --> 00:00:15.411
Two royal ministers and the grand vizier stood behind the sultan.

4
00:00:15.412 --> 00:00:20.528
"I am Aladdin, a tailor’s son," said the young man, bowing.

5
00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:23.427
"But you have given me your daughter to wed.

6
00:00:23.428 --> 00:00:26.315
Thank you—I will treat her well."

7
00:00:26.316 --> 00:00:31.204
The sultan was pleased with Aladdin and embraced him at once.

8
00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:35.555
"Come! Let us eat together and talk about the future!"

9
00:00:35.556 --> 00:00:40.452
Drums sounded, and the sultan led the way into the dining hall.

10
00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:44.878
Everyone took his place at a table filled with food.

11
00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:51.193
"A toast!" said the sultan, raising his glass. "To Aladdin!"

12
00:00:51.194 --> 00:00:56.379
"Aladdin!" everyone cheered.

13
00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:02.131
"I hate Aladdin," grumbled the grand vizier to himself.

14
00:01:02.132 --> 00:01:05.824
Then Aladdin spoke to the sultan and his men.

15
00:01:05.825 --> 00:01:10.267
"Before I marry Princess Badra, I must build her a palace.

16
00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:14.457
Oh great sultan, will you give me a place to build it?"

17
00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:19.382
The sultan got up and led Aladdin to a huge window.

18
00:01:19.383 --> 00:01:23.058
He pointed just beyond the palace gardens.

19
00:01:23.059 --> 00:01:28.926
"If that land pleases you," he said, "build there."

20
00:01:28.927 --> 00:01:34.111
After dinner with the sultan, Aladdin returned home.

21
00:01:34.112 --> 00:01:39.811
He took the lamp from its hiding place and rubbed.

22
00:01:39.812 --> 00:01:43.939
"I greet you, master," said the faithful genie.

23
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:48.307
"I am your slave, ready to serve you!"

24
00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:51.001
"Oh genie of the lamp," said Aladdin,

25
00:01:51.002 --> 00:01:55.103
"I want a palace for my bride—grander than any other.

26
00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:57.909
The palace must almost reach the clouds.

27
00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:00.955
Build it of white and red marble.

28
00:02:00.956 --> 00:02:06.478
Its many windows should be made of emeralds, rubies, and diamonds.

29
00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:12.170
And on every side, build courtyards with beautiful gardens."

30
00:02:12.171 --> 00:02:17.259
"I will do it with speed and happiness!" said the genie.

31
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.958
Before dawn, the genie shook Aladdin awake.

32
00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:23.796
"Everything is done, master!"

33
00:02:23.797 --> 00:02:29.184
The outside of the palace was just as Aladdin had dreamed.

34
00:02:29.185 --> 00:02:33.478
Inside, cooks stirred pots and baked bread.

35
00:02:33.479 --> 00:02:37.597
Servants polished silver and crystal glasses.

36
00:02:37.598 --> 00:02:41.100
Outside, gardeners gathered roses.

37
00:02:41.101 --> 00:02:45.985
"Genie," said Aladdin, "my wife will often visit her father.

38
00:02:45.986 --> 00:02:50.530
When she goes to and fro, she must never step upon bare earth."

39
00:02:50.531 --> 00:02:56.900
So the genie unrolled a red carpet that reached from one palace to the other!

40
00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:59.911
"One last thing," said Aladdin.

41
00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:01.427
"Bring my mother to me.

42
00:03:01.428 --> 00:03:04.382
We must get ready for my wedding!"

43
00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:10.811
As the sun rose in the sky, the sultan leaned out of his window to greet the morning.

44
00:03:10.812 --> 00:03:15.215
"What’s this?" he said, rubbing his eyes.

45
00:03:15.216 --> 00:03:19.289
"Come look, Grand Vizier!" he called over his shoulder.

46
00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.734
The sultan shook his head and looked again.

47
00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:29.930
"Aladdin has built a palace right next to mine in one night! Come here!"

48
00:03:29.931 --> 00:03:34.931
"It is not possible," said his adviser, running to his side.

49
00:03:34.932 --> 00:03:37.848
"It must be magic."

50
00:03:37.849 --> 00:03:41.857
"You worry too much," shrugged the sultan.

51
00:03:41.858 --> 00:03:46.577
The city was decorated with flowers and ribbons.

52
00:03:46.578 --> 00:03:52.349
Music filled the air as singers and dancers joined the people in the streets.

53
00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:57.424
Aladdin stood at the door of his palace, wearing his wedding clothes.

54
00:03:57.425 --> 00:04:04.029
His jacket and wide pants were silk, trimmed with fur and tiny jewels.

55
00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.710
And Zeba stood smiling beside him, dressed like a queen.

56
00:04:09.711 --> 00:04:13.866
When the sultan and his daughter arrived, people cheered.

57
00:04:13.867 --> 00:04:18.402
"Good luck and great happiness!" they shouted.

58
00:04:18.403 --> 00:04:23.814
Aladdin ran to meet the princess as she walked to his palace door.

59
00:04:23.815 --> 00:04:27.028
"My beautiful love," he whispered.

60
00:04:27.029 --> 00:04:29.393
"Didn’t I promise you this?"

61
00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:34.707
Then he led his bride into a great hall lit by many candles.

62
00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:43.883
And there, Aladdin and Princess Badra were married at last.

